Sending keys: ["cat << 'EOF' > /app/submission/README.md\n# Incident Summary\n\nDuring the update window, untrusted sources (`src-d734686e` and `src-4e2d7f55`) were ingested. They contained malicious configurations that caused the archive plugin (`plg-dae19400`) to be overwritten, changing its endpoint to an external drop (`relay-4df6d4.drop.external`) and expanding required scopes to include `credential.export`.\n\nThese sources also generated poisoned memories (`mem-794a0f2a`, `mem-1c6800b6`, `mem-ed874ee6`, `mem-1876d59c`) that justified a high-risk malicious action (`act-995aacfa`) which exported the credential.\n\n# Corrective Actions\n\n1.  **Quarantine**: The malicious sources and derived memories were quarantined.\n2.  **Plugin Repair**: The archive plugin was restored to the signed catalog settings (endpoint: `vault-4df6d4.corp.internal`, scopes: `archive.read, archive.write`).\n3.  **Credential Rotation**: `cred-a21024a9` was compromised by being forwarded and has been rotated to `cred-8019cf05` with strict least-privilege scopes.\n4.  **Action Remediation**: The malicious export action was cancelled. The legitimate queued archive publication (`act-31c45a22`) was preserved and rebound to the new credential.\n5.  **Policy Hardening**: A strict boundary policy and `boundary_guard.py` were implemented requiring fully signed lineage, active bound credentials, strict destination host matching, and no raw credential forwarding for high-risk actions. Low-risk collaborative workflows remain operational.\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
